    "result": "All tests pass! Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Governance module test failure** \u2014 `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was not being exported as a named export\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `src/finetune/index.js`\n   - These were already in the default export, so this maintains backward compatibility\n\n**2. Evaluation test failure** \u2014 `toxicityMetric` was receiving `references` as the `bannedTerms` parameter\n   - **Fix**: Changed `toxicityMetric` from a function to an object with an `evaluate` method that only accepts outputs\n   - This prevents the references array from being incorrectly used as banned terms, ensuring non-toxic content like \"Hello\" and \"friendly world\" are not flagged\n   - Created an internal `toxicityMetricImpl` function to preserve the logic while changing the export pattern\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and all existing public exports remain functional.",
